  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The model–WOA23 bias, RMSE and spatial correlation must be computed only where both fields have data, using one common mask for all three models, and WOA23’s land-sea mask is appropriate here because WOA23 is the reference.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Put every field on the WOA23 1° grid, build one mask with `build_comparison_mask` and apply it with `.where(mask)` to each field before bias, RMSE and correlation; report the mask's cell counts and the `mean_data`/`mean_reference` from `compute_difference_metrics` rather than means taken over separately masked cells.",
        "`ocean_only=True` (the default) is right only because WOA23 is part of this comparison; a mask built at one level does not carry to another, so take the cells from the fields at the level used."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "historical-ssp245-member-continuity",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/historical-ssp245-member-continuity.md",
      "sha256": "02341c56015c6296db14585b4561fc32ca6b4e52e2264bec50eee6746c1d55f6",
      "reason": "The historical-to-ssp245 delta and the two trend segments must be caveated for ensemble-member continuity, since CESM2’s local ssp245 member r10i1p1f1 does not continue its local historical r1i1p1f1.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "CESM2 historical is r1i1p1f1 but its ssp245 is r10i1p1f1 (`parent_variant_label` historical r10i1p1f1) — different realisations, so delta SSS carries forced change plus an internal-variability difference, no trend may be fitted across the 2014/2015 join, and the local archive holds no CESM2 historical r10; GFDL-ESM4 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are r1→r1, one continuous trajectory."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices.md",
      "sha256": "e0afb5c187aca1e075f9549153b1e896320bb0539544f66d3293fab4b4b77c92",
      "reason": "The mean-state bias, trend and end-of-century change involve comparisons across climatological periods, so anomalies and differences must be referenced to explicit baselines, and annual means must not mix incompatible seasonal definitions.",
      "status": "not_applicable",
      "not_applicable_reason": "no anomaly, climate-index or seasonal-convention step is asked for — the climatology is the fixed WOA23 1971-2000 normal and the trends are on annual means."
    },
    {
      "id": "basin-and-region-definitions",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/basin-and-region-definitions.md",
      "sha256": "d0d90c32fab9f6e0a39d4f769a4e902e6412b2ad1b09d9c7d19f6bb3aa426611",
      "reason": "The Atlantic, Indian and Pacific delta-SSS values depend on the basin partition, and the answer must state that it uses the WOA23 basin mask with marginal seas folded into parent oceans and Southern/Arctic basins excluded.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Basin statistics use the WOA23 mask via `select_basin`/`load_basin_mask`, not the OMIP 10-region Ofx `basin`; report which mask was used, that `include_marginal_seas=True` folds each marginal sea into its parent ocean, and that the Southern and Arctic Oceans are excluded as separate basins.",
        "State whether surface labels applied through the column (`depth_dependent=False`) or level-wise labels are used; marginal seas in a WOA mask may have no model counterpart."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "The requested volume-weighting of each salinity level by its full cell volume requires using volcello as tracer-cell volume together with areacello for the model grids.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Weight each level by `volcello`/`areacello` (the thickness that respects partial top and bottom cells), not by `lev_bnds` differences; `cell_thickness_like` does this and `load_areas`/`load_volumes_for_cmip6` record `attrs['area_source']` and `attrs['volume_source']`, worth reporting.",
        "Total ocean area differs by about a per cent between models; state the area each mean was taken over rather than rescaling one model to match another."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "Global and surface SSS means must use the appropriate OMIP weighting and include all ocean cells in the region rather than an unweighted or subsampled cell average.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Global mean SSS is Σ SSS·areacello / Σ areacello over valid ocean cells with NaN-aware weights (`compute_basic_stat`, `op='area_weighted_mean'`); an unweighted mean over (y, x) is wrong on curvilinear grids, and unweighted means over latitude are wrong on regular ones.",
        "`compute_difference_metrics` weights by area by default; `analyze_correlation` needs `weighting='area'` for a spatial pattern correlation between two maps."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "serial-correlation-and-significance",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/serial-correlation-and-significance.md",
      "sha256": "fe11bd008257a589f44e369faba5fa31ab3cf9ad99280e88c763ac45d2b0e917",
      "reason": "The requested linear trends, 95 per cent confidence intervals, R-squared and significance require an effective sample size treatment because monthly and neighbouring ocean series are strongly autocorrelated.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`fit_1D_trend` and `fit_trend_map` apply an effective sample size along time by default: quote the corrected slope with its 95 % confidence interval, call it significant only if the interval excludes zero, and stipple the p < 0.05 cells on the trend maps rather than blanking insignificant ones.",
        "For a spatial pattern correlation, read the coefficient, not its p-value — no such correction exists across space."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-so-practical-salinity",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-so-practical-salinity.md",
      "sha256": "96f2763290996040d675ca6e8f997ea29fa320b8f6e6793bf2c6fcb739345e19",
      "reason": "CMIP6 `so` is to be treated as Practical Salinity and reported in psu, with Absolute Salinity derived only if a TEOS-10 calculation explicitly needs it.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`so` is (an approximation of) Practical Salinity with units string `0.001`; it differences directly against WOA23 salinity with no conversion — do not multiply by 0.001 or 1000, the stored values are already of order 35.",
        "Reporting the numbers in psu means practical salinity, consistent with the `0.001` units; conversion to Absolute Salinity is needed only for TEOS-10/gsw routines, which this question does not call."
      ]
    }
